    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d926">

                <pb facs="0870" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/93</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.17 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1902. Swedish press reports Finnish press bureau wires Count von der
                        Goltz reports April 13 Helsingfors been stormed after three days’
                    desperate fighting. Several thousand prisoners and great quantity booty
                    captured, enemy offering desperate resistance. White prisoners were
                    liberated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Morris</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
